WEBVTT

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:03.150
In the ruins in the foggy skies above the clouds,

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:05.550
Jinlong, the Number's spirit, and Kaito

00:00:05.550 --> 00:00:08.240
have started a Duel with each other’s Dragons at stake.

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:14.290
But Jinlong places one wall of challenges after another in Kaito's way.

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:21.240
It's looking bad for Kaito...

00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:24.920
Drain Dragon’s current Attack Power is 8000.

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:27.490
If Galaxy-Eyes gets attacked...

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:30.720
Also, when Drain Dragon gets destroyed...

00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:36.620
...the opponent will take half of its Attack Points, meaning 4000 points, as damage.

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:40.810
If this goes on, Kaito won't be able to even touch him...!

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:43.430
Now, what will you do, Kaito?

00:00:44.530 --> 00:00:46.160
Just get on with it!

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:54.370
Relax! During the turn Drain Dragon is Special Summoned, it cannot attack.

00:00:54.470 --> 00:00:55.520
Say what?

00:00:55.610 --> 00:00:56.980
Then Kaito is...

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:59.870
I'll end my turn with this.

00:01:00.550 --> 00:01:03.120
Seems you just escaped death there!

00:01:03.310 --> 00:01:07.250
Are you... trying to mock me?!

00:01:07.670 --> 00:01:11.950
Don’t get the wrong idea. This is no more than a trial for you.

00:01:11.990 --> 00:01:14.040
A mere wall that's in your way.

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:18.440
I want to see how you will get over it.

00:01:20.870 --> 00:01:23.550
So if you can't overcome it,

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:26.270
you will be swallowed by that wall.

00:01:26.290 --> 00:01:29.920
Stop joking! My turn! Draw!

00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:32.640
Somehow he survived, but...

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:37.460
That's right. If Kaito doesn't manage to break through this situation this turn...

00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:39.120
... he will lose.

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:42.180
Now, what's up, Kaito?

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:46.470
I activate the Magic Card, Desperate Scrape!

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:49.520
With this card, I pay 800 of my Life,

00:01:54.350 --> 00:01:58.270
to halve the original Attack Power of one opposing Monster!

00:01:58.750 --> 00:02:01.550
Drain Dragon's original Attack Power is 4000,

00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:03.810
so it goes down by 2000 points!

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:08.490
Then, Drain Dragon has the same amount of my Life Points added to its Attack Power.

00:02:09.240 --> 00:02:12.720
Since my Life has been reduced, its Attack Power goes down!

00:02:13.610 --> 00:02:18.550
No way! Kaito cut down his own Life in order to lower that thing's Attack Power?

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:24.470
Oh! But Drain Dragon's Attack Power still is 5200.

00:02:24.470 --> 00:02:26.490
You still haven't overcome the wall!

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:30.500
Then I activate the Magic Card, Dragonic Divine!

00:02:31.180 --> 00:02:35.270
When there is a Level Eight or higher Dragon-Type Monster on my field,

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:39.040
I can pay 1000 Life...

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:44.470
...to return the Magic Card I last used this turn
from my Graveyard back to my hand.

00:02:45.950 --> 00:02:49.640
I'll retrieve Desperate Scrape!

00:02:50.380 --> 00:02:52.180
Then, since my Life was reduced,

00:02:52.490 --> 00:02:55.470
Drain Dragon's Attack Power is reduced again!

00:02:55.870 --> 00:02:57.550
Kaito lost even more Life...

00:02:57.780 --> 00:02:59.090
As expected...

00:03:00.920 --> 00:03:03.520
He instantly comes up with a counter measure...

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:08.350
What are you saying? Now he's only got 2200 Life left...

00:03:08.490 --> 00:03:12.320
No, he'll have no more than 200 Life left.

00:03:12.410 --> 00:03:12.740
Huh?

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:17.240
Then I activate the Magic Card, Desperate Scrape, again!

00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:19.690
I pay 800 of my Life...

00:03:21.490 --> 00:03:25.550
...to halve the original Attack Power of the opposing Monster!

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:29.780
Drain Dragon's original Attack Power was 2000,

00:03:29.870 --> 00:03:31.670
so it goes 1000 points down!

00:03:33.010 --> 00:03:35.120
Then, as my Life has been further reduced,

00:03:35.350 --> 00:03:37.010
he loses 800 Attack Points!

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:40.470
Now Galaxy-Eyes' Attack Power is higher!

00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:44.980
Go, Galaxy-Eyes! Attack Drain Dragon!

00:03:45.290 --> 00:03:48.180
Photon Stream of Destruction!!

00:03:59.810 --> 00:04:01.550
My Life...!

00:04:01.780 --> 00:04:03.610
You did it, Kaito!

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:04.290
But...

00:04:04.870 --> 00:04:08.520
At this moment, Drain Dragon's effect activates!

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:11.400
When this Monster has been destroyed,

00:04:11.630 --> 00:04:16.830
half of its current Attack Power is is inflicted to the opponent as damage.

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:24.800
Kaito!

00:04:29.930 --> 00:04:32.170
Kaito only has 200 Life left...

00:04:32.870 --> 00:04:34.130
You mean...

00:04:34.230 --> 00:04:36.330
Yeah, I already figured it out a while ago.

00:04:36.700 --> 00:04:41.800
This was probably the only way to defeat the 8000 Attack Power Drain Dragon.

00:04:41.930 --> 00:04:42.600
True.

00:04:42.830 --> 00:04:46.300
What the heck? Are you saying I'm the only one down at my level who didn't know?

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:50.200
Don't you worry. We are fully aware of that.

00:04:50.670 --> 00:04:53.970
Shut up! There are things even I know!

00:04:54.030 --> 00:04:54.730
And that is?

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:57.870
That is, that Kaito will win!

00:04:58.600 --> 00:05:02.170
But his remaining Life is a mere 200...

00:05:03.070 --> 00:05:04.200
Indeed...

00:05:28.030 --> 00:05:35.580
<i>Being best friends doesn't mean we always were</i>

00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:38.630
<i>That's pretty much true</i>

00:05:38.920 --> 00:05:46.090
<i>I found you during our serious battles</i>

00:05:46.260 --> 00:05:49.640
<i>The other me inside myself</i>

00:05:49.640 --> 00:05:54.520
<i>Awakening from within the conflict</i>

00:05:54.520 --> 00:06:00.860
<i>A turn for a chance! Seize it! Draw!</i>

00:06:00.860 --> 00:06:04.070
<i>Duel! Dualism!</i>

00:06:04.070 --> 00:06:06.950
<i>These cards are polished to fit each other</i>

00:06:06.950 --> 00:06:11.580
<i>My fated opponent is my heart reflected through the mirror</i>

00:06:11.580 --> 00:06:14.660
<i>And if we end up with a "tie" in the end,</i>

00:06:14.660 --> 00:06:23.130
<i>when we fall, all covered with mud, we'll praise each other</i>

00:06:37.620 --> 00:06:42.540
Since there is no other Monster than Draggluong on my field,

00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:45.630
"The Legend of Misael! The Divine Dragon
 that Became a Number"

00:06:42.630 --> 00:06:45.090
he will appear again!

00:06:52.430 --> 00:06:55.060
Trap, activate! Killing Reward!

00:06:55.890 --> 00:07:00.850
With this card, when my opponent’s Monster was destroyed
and that Monster was Level Seven or higher

00:07:01.060 --> 00:07:03.060
I can draw two cards!

00:07:03.230 --> 00:07:05.480
The destroyed Drain Dragon was Level Eight!

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:08.440
so I draw two cards!

00:07:11.030 --> 00:07:14.120
I set two cards and end my turn!

00:07:14.620 --> 00:07:18.120
You  seem to have overcome Drain Dragon's test,

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:22.120
but the last "wall” won't be that easy!

00:07:23.710 --> 00:07:26.710
My turn! Draw!

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:30.130
I activate Draggluong's effect!

00:07:30.340 --> 00:07:33.140
When this Monster has no Overlay Units,

00:07:33.220 --> 00:07:37.430
and no other Dragon-Type Monsters 
apart from this card are on my field,

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:41.980
I can take control of one Dragon-Type Monster
 on my opponent's field.

00:07:46.020 --> 00:07:49.650
I shall receive your soul, Galaxy-Eyes!

00:07:50.190 --> 00:07:54.660
But with this effect, you can pay half of your Life...

00:07:54.870 --> 00:07:58.830
then it will be negated and Galaxy-Eyes will be destroyed.

00:08:04.960 --> 00:08:08.920
I can't use our Barian power here.
 Just what is <i>with</i> this mountain...?

00:08:11.090 --> 00:08:13.680
What’s... this feeling?!

00:08:14.050 --> 00:08:16.800
No way...! Kaito let his Galaxy-Eyes...!

00:08:17.010 --> 00:08:20.890
You should know the power of your Galaxy-Eyes better than anyone.

00:08:21.020 --> 00:08:24.350
You can choose to destroy it with your own hands if you like.

00:08:24.560 --> 00:08:28.270
Rather than leave him in enemy hands,
 shouldn't you choose to destroy him?

00:08:28.320 --> 00:08:29.820
You couldn't possibly understand.

00:08:30.530 --> 00:08:33.360
The strength of the bond between me and Galaxy-Eyes.

00:08:33.780 --> 00:08:36.320
Galaxy-Eyes doesn't exist without me...

00:08:36.740 --> 00:08:38.990
...nor do I exist without Galaxy-Eyes.

00:08:39.740 --> 00:08:41.450
All the more, I'm telling you...

00:08:41.660 --> 00:08:44.420
...it's impossible for me to destroy Galaxy-Eyes!

00:08:45.710 --> 00:08:49.340
Then your Galaxy-Eyes will fall into my hands!

00:08:49.750 --> 00:08:52.380
Do it, Draggluong!

00:08:59.560 --> 00:09:02.100
Now Galaxy-Eyes is Kaito's enemy!

00:09:02.270 --> 00:09:06.980
As an act of sympathy, I will at least
 finish you off with your own Monster.

00:09:07.860 --> 00:09:09.770
Go, Galaxy-Eyes!

00:09:09.860 --> 00:09:12.150
Direct Attack on Kaito!

00:09:13.070 --> 00:09:13.940
Kaito...

00:09:14.360 --> 00:09:15.450
What are you planning to do?

00:09:15.820 --> 00:09:16.660
Kaito!

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:20.450
Continuous Trap, activate! Destiny Break!

00:09:20.530 --> 00:09:24.040
With this card, if an opposing Monster declares a Direct Attack,

00:09:24.460 --> 00:09:26.330
I can draw one card!

00:09:26.790 --> 00:09:29.130
And if that card is a Monster Card,

00:09:29.250 --> 00:09:31.250
that battle will be negated!

00:09:31.710 --> 00:09:33.210
What I drew is...

00:09:34.260 --> 00:09:37.260
...the Monster Card, Galaxy Knight!

00:09:41.720 --> 00:09:43.930
So you Duel relying on luck?

00:09:44.230 --> 00:09:46.390
It's not luck! It's inevitability!

00:09:46.730 --> 00:09:47.850
What did you say?!

00:09:47.900 --> 00:09:52.610
The best Duelists can even guide the cards they draw!

00:09:53.650 --> 00:09:56.450
Those are the bonds between me and Galaxy-Eyes!

00:09:56.860 --> 00:10:01.910
But I still have Draggluong to attack.

00:10:02.330 --> 00:10:04.160
Go, Draggluong!

00:10:04.750 --> 00:10:07.790
Direct Attack on Kaito again!

00:10:08.330 --> 00:10:10.130
Blazing Divine Attack!

00:10:11.500 --> 00:10:14.840
I activate Destiny Break's effect again!

00:10:14.960 --> 00:10:15.920
Wha-?!

00:10:16.220 --> 00:10:19.840
I draw one card from my deck!

00:10:21.100 --> 00:10:24.140
I've drawn one more Galaxy Knight!

00:10:24.970 --> 00:10:27.480
So Draggluong's effect is negated!

00:10:28.230 --> 00:10:29.480
Impossible!

00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:33.360
Then Destiny Break's other effect activates!

00:10:34.150 --> 00:10:36.860
When the battles are over, this card gets destroyed,

00:10:37.150 --> 00:10:42.320
and then I Special Summon the Monsters I drew with this card's effect with their effects negated!

00:10:43.490 --> 00:10:46.450
I Special Summon the two Galaxy Knights!

00:10:48.790 --> 00:10:53.040
Tch... I set one card and end my turn!

00:10:53.460 --> 00:10:56.800
Somehow Kaito survived Jinlong's attacks.

00:10:57.090 --> 00:11:01.340
But... as it is right now, there is nothing Kaito can do.

00:11:03.550 --> 00:11:06.220
My turn. Draw!

00:11:10.140 --> 00:11:10.850
Hmm?!

00:11:12.060 --> 00:11:15.320
I activate the Magic Card, Destiny Overlay!

00:11:16.030 --> 00:11:18.860
This card lets me use Monsters from my opponent's field...

00:11:19.030 --> 00:11:23.320
and Monsters from my field for an Xyz Summon!

00:11:23.660 --> 00:11:24.780
What did you say?!

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:28.000
Using the opponent's Monsters for an Xyz Summon?

00:11:28.660 --> 00:11:31.460
I use the two Level Eight Galaxy Knights...

00:11:32.330 --> 00:11:35.710
...together with the Galaxy-Eyes on your field for an Overlay!

00:11:35.960 --> 00:11:39.130
With these three Monsters, I build the Overlay Network!

00:11:39.260 --> 00:11:40.590
Xyz Summon!

00:11:41.760 --> 00:11:45.550
Great Galaxy of Reversal, become a surging wave of light,

00:11:45.680 --> 00:11:47.970
and show your mighty form!

00:11:50.520 --> 00:11:53.060
Descend, my very soul!

00:11:53.730 --> 00:11:56.730
Neo Galaxy-Eyes Photon Dragon!

00:12:08.120 --> 00:12:10.790
Just what is happening on that mountain top?

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:14.290
This is... a noble dragon's roar.

00:12:15.540 --> 00:12:18.590
There are two dragons fighting...

00:12:22.340 --> 00:12:25.300
Neo Galaxy-Eyes Photon Dragon...

00:12:26.260 --> 00:12:28.470
So you took back your Monster,

00:12:28.680 --> 00:12:30.680
and then evolved it?

00:12:31.230 --> 00:12:34.230
Now he can activate Neo Galaxy-eyes’ effect!

00:12:34.230 --> 00:12:34.730
No.

00:12:34.730 --> 00:12:35.150
Huh?

00:12:35.650 --> 00:12:37.360
Have you forgotten, Kaito?

00:12:37.770 --> 00:12:40.480
As long as Draggluong is on the field,

00:12:40.610 --> 00:12:46.740
the effects of Dragon-Type Monsters
 on the opponent's field are negated!

00:12:46.990 --> 00:12:49.330
Neo Galaxy-Eyes’ effect has been sealed!

00:12:49.790 --> 00:12:52.500
Also, Draggluong is a Number,

00:12:53.370 --> 00:12:56.040
and Numbers can only be destroyed by other Numbers.

00:12:58.170 --> 00:13:00.550
And with Draggluong's effect,

00:13:00.550 --> 00:13:05.090
next turn, Neo Galaxy-Eyes will be mine.

00:13:05.470 --> 00:13:09.260
No way! That means Kaito has to settle it this turn?!

00:13:09.260 --> 00:13:09.970
Be quiet!

00:13:10.720 --> 00:13:12.100
Just shut up and watch!

00:13:12.560 --> 00:13:14.060
But.. if this goes on...

00:13:14.390 --> 00:13:16.730
My victory has already been decided.

00:13:17.730 --> 00:13:18.730
What?!

00:13:19.110 --> 00:13:22.990
I activate Overlay Sniper's effect from my Graveyard!

00:13:23.690 --> 00:13:25.860
By Banishing this card from the Graveyard,

00:13:26.110 --> 00:13:30.700
I select one Xyz Monster on my field and for every Overlay Unit it has,

00:13:30.780 --> 00:13:33.950
the Attack Power of one opposing Monster lowers by 500!

00:13:34.710 --> 00:13:37.420
Neo Galaxy-Eyes has three Overlay Units,

00:13:37.580 --> 00:13:39.590
so it goes down by 1500 Points!

00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:44.010
Then I activate Overlay Booster's effect from my graveyard!

00:13:44.470 --> 00:13:46.260
By Banishing this card from the Graveyard,

00:13:47.260 --> 00:13:52.060
I select one Xyz Monster on my field and for each Overlay Unit it has,

00:13:52.220 --> 00:13:54.430
its Attack Power goes up by 500 points!

00:13:54.730 --> 00:13:59.190
Therefore, Neo Galaxy-Eyes' Attack Power goes up by 1500 points!

00:13:59.860 --> 00:14:01.070
What?!

00:14:01.400 --> 00:14:02.650
Awesome, Kaito!

00:14:02.940 --> 00:14:06.070
Go, Neo Galaxy-Eyes Photon Dragon!

00:14:06.400 --> 00:14:08.360
Destroy Draggluong!

00:14:09.240 --> 00:14:13.740
Don't underestimate me! Trap, activate! Dragon Dance!

00:14:14.870 --> 00:14:19.710
When a Dragon-Type Xyz Monster on my field is attacked,

00:14:19.920 --> 00:14:22.420
I can Banish two Dragon-Type Monsters from my Graveyard,

00:14:22.800 --> 00:14:28.430
then Neo Galaxy-Eyes loses Attack Points equal to their total combined Attack Points!

00:14:29.220 --> 00:14:34.060
I Banish Protect Dragon and Drain Dragon!

00:14:34.970 --> 00:14:38.480
The total combined Attack Points of these two Dragons is 6000,

00:14:39.020 --> 00:14:43.520
therefore Neo Galaxy-Eyes' Attack Power will go down by 6000!

00:14:44.070 --> 00:14:46.780
Neo Galaxy-Eyes' Attack Power became zero!

00:14:46.860 --> 00:14:48.150
That's bad!

00:14:48.450 --> 00:14:51.160
That’s right, you cannot stop the attack.

00:14:51.660 --> 00:14:54.660
Alright, give him the counterattack, Draggluong!

00:14:56.700 --> 00:14:58.500
Goodbye, Kaito!

00:15:00.920 --> 00:15:02.670
<i>You</i> will disappear.

00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:04.090
What?

00:15:05.050 --> 00:15:08.470
I activate the Counter Trap, Galaxy Dragon Rain!

00:15:09.340 --> 00:15:13.010
With this card, when Dragon-Type Xyz Monsters battle,

00:15:13.550 --> 00:15:17.390
the activation and effects of my opponent’s Trap Cards are negated!

00:15:21.230 --> 00:15:22.810
Im... Impossible!

00:15:23.110 --> 00:15:25.440
I haven’t underestimated you at all.

00:15:25.610 --> 00:15:27.570
With your absolute knowledge of Dragons,

00:15:27.570 --> 00:15:31.530
the tactics you tormented me with brought the best out of me.

00:15:31.820 --> 00:15:35.620
That's why I set this card in order to honor you for that.

00:15:35.780 --> 00:15:36.580
Kaito...

00:15:37.160 --> 00:15:39.540
Take this blow from us!

00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:44.540
Ultimate Photon Stream!

00:16:02.140 --> 00:16:04.230
You did it, Kaito!

00:16:12.400 --> 00:16:14.820
Indeed, a very interesting Duel.

00:16:15.030 --> 00:16:17.330
Why were you testing me like that?

00:16:17.450 --> 00:16:22.830
Before I answer your question, 
let me tell you the legend of this place.

00:16:23.370 --> 00:16:24.960
Misael's legend?

00:16:25.250 --> 00:16:25.790
Huh?

00:16:26.290 --> 00:16:27.090
Right...

00:16:27.790 --> 00:16:33.260
A long long time ago, this land was protected by a single dragon.

00:16:34.220 --> 00:16:38.060
In particular though, the hero of this land, Misael, and the dragon...

00:16:38.060 --> 00:16:41.810
...were able to truly understand each other's hearts, thus becoming partners..

00:16:41.930 --> 00:16:45.150
...and they were allies who fought side by side in Duels too.

00:16:45.850 --> 00:16:51.780
Due to Misael's and the Dragon's efforts, the days continued calmly and peaceful.

00:16:53.740 --> 00:16:58.370
But one year, a terrible disaster struck the land,

00:16:58.870 --> 00:17:02.160
and many innocent people died.

00:17:02.660 --> 00:17:06.710
At that time, a wandering shaman appeared...

00:17:06.790 --> 00:17:11.590
...spreading that it was the dragon
 that had brought disaster to the land.

00:17:11.960 --> 00:17:17.430
The people were fooled by these words and began to loathe the dragon, their Guardian Angel...

00:17:17.430 --> 00:17:19.350
...and decided to drag him down.

00:17:19.970 --> 00:17:24.730
Although Misael desperately tried to persuade the people...

00:17:24.890 --> 00:17:27.350
...his words didn't reach them.

00:17:27.850 --> 00:17:31.530
To add, they cried out that if Misael wanted to be a true hero...

00:17:31.530 --> 00:17:35.150
...he would slay the dragon, their voices echoing one after another.

00:17:35.400 --> 00:17:38.450
Finally, Misael made up his mind.

00:17:39.200 --> 00:17:43.040
He stood before the dragon and told the people this:

00:17:43.620 --> 00:17:49.080
"If I give up my life in his stead, will you believe my words?"

00:17:50.960 --> 00:17:52.130
But at this moment...

00:17:52.800 --> 00:17:57.430
... hundreds of thousands of arrows pierced through Misael and the dragon.

00:17:58.430 --> 00:18:03.220
It was the army of a neighboring country that had been waiting for this moment...

00:18:03.220 --> 00:18:05.230
...to invade this land.

00:18:05.890 --> 00:18:09.560
Yes, the Shaman was a spy from the other country,

00:18:10.110 --> 00:18:13.480
...and this land was erased.

00:18:14.570 --> 00:18:18.910
Kaito, despite whatever trial came before you,

00:18:18.950 --> 00:18:22.490
you refused to give up the power to decide your own fate.

00:18:23.330 --> 00:18:27.830
I on the other hand, gave my life, not unlike Misael...

00:18:28.120 --> 00:18:29.040
Shut up!

00:18:34.460 --> 00:18:35.920
You... You are...

00:18:36.340 --> 00:18:37.380
Misael!

00:18:41.010 --> 00:18:44.010
Mi-... Misael... You...

00:18:44.560 --> 00:18:46.520
No... There's no way...

00:18:46.930 --> 00:18:51.020
But... I can feel Misael in your soul...

00:18:51.560 --> 00:18:53.520
Could it be... You <i>are</i>...?

00:18:54.020 --> 00:18:55.280
Screw this!

00:18:58.740 --> 00:19:02.450
I am one of these worthless, lowly humans, you say!?
 Stop that nonsense!

00:19:02.780 --> 00:19:04.080
You... damn..!

00:19:04.120 --> 00:19:04.660
Wait.

00:19:05.910 --> 00:19:10.540
Wasn't I supposed to be your opponent, Misael?!

00:19:11.750 --> 00:19:12.960
Interesting.

00:19:13.630 --> 00:19:17.460
Seems like it's finally time for the two of us to settle things, Kaito!

00:19:17.630 --> 00:19:18.720
Kaito...

00:19:19.340 --> 00:19:21.010
What the heck?

00:19:24.010 --> 00:19:25.060
This is...!

00:19:26.720 --> 00:19:27.720
Watch out!

00:19:27.770 --> 00:19:29.770
I don't want to become scrap!

00:19:36.690 --> 00:19:38.400
I'll pull back for today.

00:19:38.610 --> 00:19:40.650
But next time, we'll finally finish this...!

00:19:42.160 --> 00:19:43.030
Misael...

00:19:43.950 --> 00:19:46.030
Wha- what the heck's going on!?

00:19:52.830 --> 00:19:54.330
He- here...?

00:19:56.250 --> 00:19:58.300
The ruins disappeared...!

00:19:59.130 --> 00:20:01.130
And on top that, that Jinlong bastard too...

00:20:08.140 --> 00:20:09.430
Dad's coin...

00:20:10.600 --> 00:20:12.640
That legend still goes on...

00:20:13.900 --> 00:20:18.610
That dragon's Soul was touched by the Number and was revived...

00:20:19.440 --> 00:20:23.070
...and until today, protected this place.

00:20:28.540 --> 00:20:32.160
Kaito. I said that I tested you.

00:20:32.620 --> 00:20:34.330
Indeed, this is true.

00:20:36.330 --> 00:20:42.130
When those seeking the Numbers of the ruins appear, a great change will happen to this world.

00:20:43.130 --> 00:20:48.430
Young Dragon Tamer, help lead the world down the right path.

00:20:49.560 --> 00:20:50.890
The right path...

00:20:52.230 --> 00:20:54.100
I saw something once...

00:20:54.440 --> 00:20:59.440
Far, far away, two divine lights were fighting in the sky.

00:21:03.820 --> 00:21:07.280
That battle lasted for hundreds of days.

00:21:08.280 --> 00:21:13.000
Rains of fire poured down on the grounds as lightning ripped through the very Earth.

00:21:13.500 --> 00:21:17.670
Then those two lights finally collided, and vanished.

00:21:20.250 --> 00:21:22.760
<i>Is this my memory?</i>

00:21:23.800 --> 00:21:27.260
<i>That I once fought the Barians?</i>

00:21:30.060 --> 00:21:34.140
Kaito, I will entrust this Number to you.

00:21:36.690 --> 00:21:40.820
That foolish battle lead this entire planet to ruin once.

00:21:42.360 --> 00:21:45.400
It must never be allowed to happen again.

00:21:54.580 --> 00:21:55.540
That's right...

00:21:56.290 --> 00:21:57.620
So that's it...

00:21:59.540 --> 00:22:01.550
I was finally able to remember.

00:22:02.590 --> 00:22:04.010
My mission is...

00:22:05.630 --> 00:22:07.930
...to destroy the Barian World.

00:22:21.110 --> 00:22:23.610
<i>Is it the world that's boring?</i>

00:22:23.610 --> 00:22:26.150
<i>Or maybe you're the one who's not gettin' serious?</i>

00:22:26.150 --> 00:22:27.360
<i>Do you understand?</i>

00:22:27.360 --> 00:22:28.780
<i>Do I understand?</i>

00:22:28.990 --> 00:22:31.660
<i>Already got my answers</i>

00:22:31.700 --> 00:22:34.160
<i>Once you start movin', you ain't stoppin'</i>

00:22:34.160 --> 00:22:36.710
<i>I go on thinkin' even while losin'.</i>

00:22:36.710 --> 00:22:37.790
<i>Do you understand?</i>

00:22:37.790 --> 00:22:38.830
<i>I understand!</i>

00:22:38.830 --> 00:22:42.210
<i>Our formula for reversal's already gathered</i>

00:22:42.210 --> 00:22:44.550
<i>You afraid it ain't comin' true?</i>

00:22:44.550 --> 00:22:47.670
<i>I gotta 'least give it a try</i>

00:22:47.670 --> 00:22:49.890
<i>Ain't no problem if they say I'm borin'</i>

00:22:49.890 --> 00:22:52.890
<i>True failure's when we stop movin'</i>

00:22:53.050 --> 00:22:54.850
<i>Come on! Ga, ga, ga, guys & dolls</i>

00:22:54.850 --> 00:22:56.220
<i>Go, go, go, go my way</i>

00:22:56.220 --> 00:22:58.100
<i>Oh, oh, oh, over ray</i>

00:22:58.390 --> 00:23:02.400
<i>Door's always open for you</i>

00:23:02.560 --> 00:23:07.490
<i>Bring your power forth and go way, go way</i>

00:23:07.490 --> 00:23:08.740
<i>I understand!</i>

00:23:08.740 --> 00:23:12.740
<i>And tears are no way, no way</i>

00:23:13.240 --> 00:23:18.120
<i>With all my strength, pave way, go way</i>

00:23:18.120 --> 00:23:19.330
<i>I understand!</i>

00:23:19.330 --> 00:23:23.460
<i>Got all the courage here</i>

00:23:23.460 --> 00:23:25.630
<i>You ought to understand!</i>

00:23:25.630 --> 00:23:27.840
<i>Go way, go way</i>

00:23:40.390 --> 00:23:42.520
I saw Gilag's face on TV!

00:23:42.560 --> 00:23:45.860
Apparently they found a stone statue that looks exactly like him!

00:23:45.980 --> 00:23:48.940
Then, the airship has shown the location of the ruins.

00:23:48.990 --> 00:23:51.950
Huh? The next location is... the Duel Lodge?!

00:23:52.200 --> 00:23:54.070
The legend is about Gilag...

00:23:54.370 --> 00:23:56.990
What the...?! The statue speaks?!

00:23:57.040 --> 00:23:58.410
They've switched bodies?!

00:23:58.450 --> 00:24:00.080
It's a tanuki Number!

00:24:00.580 --> 00:24:02.460
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZeXal II:

00:24:02.580 --> 00:24:05.920
"Yuma Confused!? The Unreliable Account of Gilag the Raccoon Dog."

00:24:06.250 --> 00:24:08.670
Yuma, your face has...
